DOCUMENT();
loadMacros(
"PGstandard.pl",
"MathObjects.pl",
"PGML.pl"
);
Context("Vector");

BEGIN_PGML
# Questions:

_For arithmetic problems, if the result is not an integer, then retain *three significant digits*._

Suppose the vectors:
- [` \vec{u} = \langle 10, 8, -7, 7 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{v} = \langle -8, 4, 9, 1 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{w} = \langle 3, -1, -9, -5 \rangle `]

Compute:
- [` \left\| \vec{v} \right\| = `] [_____]{norm(Compute("<-8, 4, 9, 1>"))}
- [` \vec{w} \cdot \vec{u} = `] [_____]{Compute("<3, -1, -9, -5>") . Compute("<10, 8, -7, 7>")}
- [` \vec{v} \cdot \vec{w} = `] [_____]{Compute("<-8, 4, 9, 1>") . Compute("<3, -1, -9, -5>")}
- [` \vec{v} \times \vec{w} = `] [_____]{Compute("<-8, 4, 9, 1>") x Compute("<3, -1, -9, -5>")}
- Enter a vector in the same direction as [` \vec{v} `]. [_____]{Compute("<-8, 4, 9, 1>")->cmp(parallel=>1,sameDirection=>1)}

---

Suppose the vectors:
- [` \vec{u} = \langle 3, -10, -1, -10 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{v} = \langle -5, 4, 5, -6 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{w} = \langle 0, -9, 8, -5 \rangle `]

Compute:
- Enter a vector parallel to [` \vec{u} `]. [_____]{Compute("<3, -10, -1, -10>")->cmp(parallel=>1)}
- Enter a unit vector in the direction of [` \vec{u} `]. [_____]{unit(Compute("<3, -10, -1, -10>"))}
- [` \vec{w} \cdot \vec{v} = `] [_____]{Compute("<0, -9, 8, -5>") . Compute("<-5, 4, 5, -6>")}
- Enter a unit vector in the direction of [` \vec{w} `]. [_____]{unit(Compute("<0, -9, 8, -5>"))}
- [` \vec{v} \cdot \vec{u} = `] [_____]{Compute("<-5, 4, 5, -6>") . Compute("<3, -10, -1, -10>")}

---

Suppose the vectors:
- [` \vec{u} = \langle 10, -6, 0, 9 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{v} = \langle 9, 8, 6, 1 \rangle `]

Compute:
- [` \vec{u} \times \vec{v} = `] [_____]{Compute("<10, -6, 0, 9>") x Compute("<9, 8, 6, 1>")}
- [` \vec{v} \times \vec{u} = `] [_____]{Compute("<9, 8, 6, 1>") x Compute("<10, -6, 0, 9>")}
- [` \left\| \vec{u} \right\| = `] [_____]{norm(Compute("<10, -6, 0, 9>"))}
- Enter a unit vector in the direction of [` \vec{u} `]. [_____]{unit(Compute("<10, -6, 0, 9>"))}

---

Suppose the vectors:
- [` \vec{u} = \langle -4, -10, -7, -6 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{v} = \langle -3, -3, -4, -5 \rangle `]

Compute:
- Enter a vector parallel to [` \vec{v} `]. [_____]{Compute("<-3, -3, -4, -5>")->cmp(parallel=>1)}
- Enter a unit vector in the direction of [` \vec{u} `]. [_____]{unit(Compute("<-4, -10, -7, -6>"))}
- [` \left\| \vec{u} \right\| = `] [_____]{norm(Compute("<-4, -10, -7, -6>"))}
- Enter a vector in the same direction as [` \vec{v} `]. [_____]{Compute("<-3, -3, -4, -5>")->cmp(parallel=>1,sameDirection=>1)}

---

Suppose the vectors:
- [` \vec{u} = \langle -8, 7, 7, 0 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{v} = \langle 4, -5, 5, 6 \rangle `]

Compute:
- [` \left\| \vec{v} \right\| = `] [_____]{norm(Compute("<4, -5, 5, 6>"))}
- [` \vec{u} \cdot \vec{v} = `] [_____]{Compute("<-8, 7, 7, 0>") . Compute("<4, -5, 5, 6>")}
- [` \vec{u} \times \vec{v} = `] [_____]{Compute("<-8, 7, 7, 0>") x Compute("<4, -5, 5, 6>")}
- [` \vec{v} \times \vec{u} = `] [_____]{Compute("<4, -5, 5, 6>") x Compute("<-8, 7, 7, 0>")}

---

Suppose the vectors:
- [` \vec{u} = \langle -9, 2, -4, -9 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{v} = \langle -8, -5, 6, -3 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{w} = \langle 0, 9, 9, 2 \rangle `]

Compute:
- [` \vec{u} \times \vec{w} = `] [_____]{Compute("<-9, 2, -4, -9>") x Compute("<0, 9, 9, 2>")}
- Enter a vector parallel to [` \vec{w} `]. [_____]{Compute("<0, 9, 9, 2>")->cmp(parallel=>1)}
- Enter a vector parallel to [` \vec{u} `]. [_____]{Compute("<-9, 2, -4, -9>")->cmp(parallel=>1)}
- [` \vec{v} \times \vec{w} = `] [_____]{Compute("<-8, -5, 6, -3>") x Compute("<0, 9, 9, 2>")}

---
END_PGML
ENDDOCUMENT();
